.SH "SKY FLOATING POINT HARDWARE SUPPORT"
.PP
This release of the Fortran
compiler supports hardware floating point.
The hardware supported are those boards made by
SKY Computers.
.PP
.nf
.in +.5i
SKY Computers, Inc.
Foot of John Street
Lowell, Massachusetts  01852
(617) 454-6200
.in -.5i
.fi
.PP
Note that UniSoft will provide \s-1UNIX\s+1 kernel support
for SKY hardware as part of the UniSoft porting services.
Each customer must have contracted with UniSoft to have the
required software modifications made to the \s-1UNIX\s+1 kernel
before attempting to use the SKY support features of the
SVS compilers.
The SVS compilers in and of themselves
will not support the SKY floating point hardware
without the required UniSoft \s-1UNIX\s+1 modifications.
.PP
Some of the SKY Computers floating point hardware boards
will require ``downloading'' of microcode. This microcode
is written and provided by SKY Computers.
